Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Evidence=20layer=20=C2=B7=20B2A=20loop-closing?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20(signal=20polish=20+=20cross-link=20+=20hash-chained=20audit?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20trail)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

B2A.6 · Signal-back-to-lawyer notification polish
- attachItem's pushNotification now leads with sourceProvider + claimant
  in the title and includes retrieval timestamp + itemId in the body.
  Deep-links in the solicitor Work dashboard remain unchanged; case
  page can highlight the new item via itemId in a future pass.

B2A.7 · Evidence tab <-> Repository tab cross-link
- case_shell.js renderFrame() now prepends a banner above the Evidence
  iframe reading '<N> items attached in the Evidence Repository ->' with
  a live count from listAttached(). Reciprocal Repo->workspace link
  already exists via the 'Open workspace' button.

B2A.11 · Hash-chained compliance audit trail (SHA-256, tamper-evident)
- NEW case_audit_trail.js: append(caseRef, event) + verify(caseRef) +
  list + lastHash. Chain persists in case.meta.evidenceAuditTrail[].
  Uses crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256') in the browser; falls back to a
  deterministic hex hash in non-browser contexts (Node smoke tests pass).
- attachItem + removeAttached now append 'attach' / 'detach' entries.
- Repository UI gains a 'Compliance audit trail' section with per-entry
  seq/timestamp/action/summary/short-hash rows, colour-coded by action.
  'Verify chain' button recomputes hashes and marks entries green
  (verified) or red (broken).

PRE-EXISTING FIX (surfaced by B1.2 seeded attachments)
- writeRepo() wrote patches to case.<top-level> but readRepo() reads
  case.meta.<key>. Live attachments were silently lost after the first
  reload. Both writeRepo and writeChain now correctly persist under
  case.meta via updateCaseMeta({meta: newMeta}).

Cache-bust: s7a across case.html / dio.html / evidence-flights.html /
evidence-workspace.html. case_audit_trail.js now loaded before
case_evidence_repository.js in the script chain.
